8skh|n|To destroy the life of by suffocation; to deprive of the air necessary for life; to cover up closely so as to prevent breathing; to suffocate; as, to smother a child. ; To affect as by suffocation; to stife; to deprive of air by a thick covering, as of ashes, of smoke, or the like; as, to smother a fire. ; Hence, to repress the action of; to cover from public view; to suppress; to conceal; as, to smother one's displeasure. ; To be suffocated or stifled. ; To burn slowly, without sufficient air; to smolder. ; Stifling smoke; thick dust. ; A state of suppression.	n:5eh7,18,3;5e13,14,4~5e13,14,4;5eh7,18,3	N:ahyt,85,1;1z7l,56,1~ahyt,85,1;1z7l,56,1
